FALCON Post-Quantum Signature Verification
==========================================

This directory contains FALCON (Fast-Fourier Lattice-based Compact Signatures
over NTRU) post-quantum signature VERIFICATION for the Linux kernel.

FALCON is a NIST-selected post-quantum cryptographic signature algorithm
(FIPS 206 / FN-DSA standardization in progress).

Source
------
Based on PQClean reference implementation:
https://github.com/PQClean/PQClean/tree/master/crypto_sign/falcon-512

License: MIT (compatible with GPL-2.0)

Files
-----
- vrfy.c        : Signature verification logic (adapted from reference)
- codec.c       : Signature encoding/decoding (adapted from reference)
- common.c      : Common utilities (adapted from reference)
- fpr.c/fpr.h   : Floating-point replacement (adapted from reference)
- inner.h       : Internal definitions (adapted from reference)
- api.h         : API definitions (adapted from reference)
- falcon_verify.c : Kernel crypto API integration (NEW)
- Kconfig       : Kernel configuration (NEW)
- Makefile      : Build system integration (NEW)

Kernel Integration
------------------
The kernel only needs SIGNATURE VERIFICATION. Key generation and signing
happen in userspace.

Supported parameter sets:
- FALCON-512 (NIST security level 1, comparable to AES-128)
- FALCON-1024 (NIST security level 5, comparable to AES-256)

Dependencies:
- CONFIG_CRYPTO_HASH
- CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256 or CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512
- CONFIG_ASYMMETRIC_KEY_TYPE
- CONFIG_X509_CERTIFICATE_PARSER

Usage
-----
Used by:
- X.509 certificate verification (crypto/asymmetric_keys/)
- PKCS#7 signature verification
- Module signing (scripts/sign-file)
- Boot certificate validation (security/boot_certs/)
- IMA/EVM (security/integrity/)

Status
------
WORK IN PROGRESS - Not yet functional

Next steps:
1. Adapt reference code for kernel environment (remove libc dependencies)
2. Integrate with kernel crypto API (crypto_sig)
3. Add X.509 and PKCS#7 support
4. Test with boot_certs system
